Subject: [PATCH 1/5] stack_numa: NUMA_FULL_T48 shape + split thread invariant
 (DAR-LAT-3h, PROPOSED)

Lands the orchestrator half of lineup-change C3 (operator-ruled 2026-09-22,
"add the needed cpu shape"), which the registry patch pointed at but never
applied. INERT on its own: no role names the shape in this commit.

- NUMA_FULL_T48 = ("0-95", 48): same cpuset, region set and class ("full") as
  NUMA_FULL; only -t differs.
- _assert_instance_invariants: `threads > phys` stays fatal for every shape;
  `threads < phys` is fatal unless the shape is in _UNDERSUBSCRIBED_SHAPES.
  The function takes optional config/shape arguments so both branches are
  tested against synthetic entries.
- The comment states what backs the 48 (pre-BIOS bare llama-bench only) and
  names gate G1 of the DAR-LAT-3h package as the deciding measurement.

Unsigned. Part of the DAR-LAT-3h stack-change package
(epyc-root artifacts/operator/stack-change-dar-lat-3h-20260926/).

